course: dictionary
lesson: 13399
title: Formal words: henceforth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Henceforth is a formal word. It means from now on, or from this time into the future. It tells you that something starts now and keeps going.
explain: «Henceforth, the library will close at five o'clock.» The sentence says the new closing time starts today and stays. To check, swap in the words from now on. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: You will often meet henceforth in announcements, rules and old stories. «Henceforth all generations shall call me blessed» comes from the Bible. Two phrases to know are henceforth known as and henceforth and forever.
fact: Henceforth means from now on.
fact: Henceforth is an adverb, so it tells you about time: when something starts.
fact: From now on and from this time on mean nearly the same thing, but henceforth sounds more formal.
fact: Henceforth is used in formal announcements, laws and old stories.
fact: Henceforth and forever means from now on, for always.
exercise: «Henceforth, the pool will open at eight o'clock.» What does henceforth mean? | *From now on | Only on Sundays | Before lunch | Long ago
exercise: The mayor says, «Henceforth, this park is a place for everyone.» What does henceforth tell you? | The park is a secret | The park is closed today | *The rule starts now and continues | The rule was true in the past
exercise: «Henceforth the school gate will be locked at four.» Find and copy the one word that means from now on. | locked | gate | *henceforth | school
test: The king said the town would henceforth be called Silverbrook. What does henceforth mean here? | *From now on | Long ago | Very quickly | At night only
test: Which phrase could replace henceforth in «Henceforth, we will tidy up after lunch.»? | Sometimes | *From now on | Once upon a time | Yesterday
exam: Mia reads a sign: «Henceforth, bikes must use the back gate.» What does the sign mean? | The rule was only for last week | Bikes may use any gate | *The rule starts now and keeps going | The back gate is closed for ever
